{"custom_id": "47983bffc9095d02f92ce2eebf8e6b21628794e69fddb1d0", "meta": {"loop": "topk1L07", "task": "annotate_with_guidelines", "occurrence": 0, "attempt": 0, "max_tokens": 128000, "prompt_sha256": "dd8dacc14a9db6181e0a984c4dc585ed64a99ae2555024c751b21e2349e251f6", "prompt_chars": 25186}, "batch_id": "msgbatch_01438JrwSD1FeRYincbckVb2", "saved_utc": "2026-10-23T11:51:54+00:00", "message": {"id": "msg_011CgK7ZpZUKXV5EsivAvTXe", "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "I need to annotate this text about WT1 gene mutations, identifying entities and their precise character offsets by counting through the text carefully.\n\nContinuing to track character offsets through the rest of the sentence, covering \"Wilms tumour (WT)\" and the follow-up text about reviewing 100 reports of intragenic WT1 mutations and examining the accompanying clinical phenotypes.\n\nI'm now mapping offsets through the next clause about sporadic Wilms tumours with intragenic WT1 mutations, continuing into the statistic about over 90% of patients with Denys-Drash syndrome.\n\nWorking through this, I'm deciding how to annotate each disease mention: \"childhood kidney cancer\" and \"Wilms tumour (WT)\" as Specific Disease entries (with the parenthetical abbreviation treated as a separate synonymous mention), \"sporadic Wilms tumours\" also Specific Disease, and \"Denys-Drash syndrome\" as Specific Disease too. For the parenthetical gloss \"(renal nephropathy, gonadal anomaly, predisposition to WT),\" I'm treating \"renal nephropathy\" as a Disease Class (a population-level feature label), leaving \"gonadal anomaly\" unannotated as too generic, and marking \"WT\" again as Specific Disease since it refers to Wilms tumour.\n\nContinuing further, I'm annotating \"juvenile granulosa cell tumour\" and \"non-asbestos related mesothelioma\" as Specific Disease mentions, and now computing character offsets for \"desmoplastic small round cell tumour\" to annotate it the same way.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"annotations\":[{\"start\":122,\"end\":145,\"text\":\"childhood kidney cancer\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"The appositive 'Wilms tumour (WT)' identifies this phrase with one specific tumour, so it is treated as a single disease rather than a family. 'cancer' is retained under the general-term exception.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1. Specific Disease\"},{\"start\":148,\"end\":160,\"text\":\"Wilms tumour\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Named, specific childhood kidney tumour with a single defined identity.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1. Specific Disease\"},{\"start\":163,\"end\":165,\"text\":\"WT\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Abbreviation defined in parentheses for Wilms tumour, annotated as a separate synonymous mention from the long form.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 6. Synonymous mentions\"},{\"start\":313,\"end\":326,\"text\":\"Wilms tumours\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Plural reference to the specific Wilms tumour disease, not to a family of diseases.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1. Specific Disease\"},{\"start\":387,\"end\":407,\"text\":\"Denys-Drash syndrome\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Named syndrome with one defined identity; the lexicalized syndrome name is annotated as a whole.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1. Specific Disease\"},{\"start\":410,\"end\":427,\"text\":\"renal nephropathy\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Feature-list phenotype label in a parenthetical describing the syndrome in general, not a patient's diagnosed condition. Nephropathy denotes a family of kidney diseases.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1. Disease Class (feature-list negative constraint)\"},{\"start\":466,\"end\":468,\"text\":\"WT\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Abbreviation for Wilms tumour used as the complement of 'predisposition to' in the syndrome description. It names one specific disease.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1. Specific Disease; 6. Synonymous mentions\"},{\"start\":560,\"end\":590,\"text\":\"juvenile granulosa cell tumour\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Named, specific tumour entity with a single defined identity.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1. Specific Disease\"},{\"start\":593,\"end\":626,\"text\":\"non-asbestos related mesothelioma\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Specific form of mesothelioma defined by its etiologic qualifier. The full mention is preferred over the substring 'mesothelioma'.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1. Specific Disease; 5. Minimum necessary span\"},{\"start\":629,\"end\":665,\"text\":\"desmoplastic small round cell tumour\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Named, specific small round cell tumour entity with a single defined identity.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1. Specific Disease\"},{\"start\":688,\"end\":710,\"text\":\"acute myeloid leukemia\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Named, specific leukemia subtype. The full phrase is preferred over substrings.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1. Specific Disease; 5. Minimum necessary span\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 9400, "output_tokens": 15290, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 14094}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}